# The deploy proxy in the serving container (#955), installed as
# /etc/caddy/Caddyfile by install.sh. cloudflared sends every request here,
# and Caddy forwards it to the API color that serves (blue on
# 127.0.0.1:8081, green on 127.0.0.1:8082). Loopback only and plain HTTP:
# TLS ends at Cloudflare's edge, and the tunnel carries the request here.
#
# update-api.sh switches colors once the new one's /readyz passes: it
# rewrites /etc/usnm-serving/upstream.caddy and runs `systemctl reload
# caddy`. Requests in flight finish on the old color.
#
# Headers: Caddy passes the request's own headers on (Host, Origin,
# Sec-Fetch-Site, CF-Connecting-IP, which the API reads), and sets
# X-Forwarded-For to its peer, cloudflared on loopback, since no proxy is
# trusted here. Caddy writes no access log unless a `log` directive asks
# for one, so no client IP or query string is logged here (09 §9.4.2).
{
	admin 127.0.0.1:2019
	auto_https off
}

http://:8080 {
	bind 127.0.0.1
	import /etc/usnm-serving/upstream.caddy
}
